        "notes": "THE HAND IS PART OF THE CODE HERE. Every row is printed as '...D/S' - Destra / Sinistra - so an order carries AU090D or AU090S, not AU090D/S. This is the first place in the registry where handedness lives INSIDE the article code instead of beside it as the per-order hinge_side axis; the generator must resolve the suffix from the chosen hand and must never emit the D/S template as an orderable code. Printed rules, verbatim: W.100/105 unit with 30 cm door - 90 cm carcass; W.115/120 unit with 45 cm door - 90 cm carcass; W.130/135 unit with 60 cm door - 120 cm carcass. UNDECODED: what the two numbers of the W notation measure. Evidence so far - the second number is always depth + 80 mm (350->430, 620->700, 670->750), which matches the 8x8 fixed corner panel; the first is 1000/1150/1300 at d.35 and d.62 but 1050/1200/1350 at d.67, i.e. +50 with the depth, which a simple carcass+panel sum does not explain. Do not model a footprint from a guess.",
